# Digested assets from `mix assets.deploy` (phx.digest), generated at release
# build time. The undigested build outputs priv/static/assets/app.{js,css} (and
# favicon.ico / robots.txt) ARE committed so the app serves with no build step;
# only the hashed copies, gzips, and manifest are generated artifacts.
#
# **Scoped to `assets/`, and it has to be.** This was `/priv/static/**/*-[0-9a-f]*.*`,
# which reads as "a hash suffix" and actually means "a hyphen followed by any of
# a-f or a digit, anywhere". `mix docs.publish` copies `docs/` and `ux/` under
# `priv/static`, so that rule silently swallowed nine of them — every
# `polyphony-admin.html`, `polyphony-browse.html`, `design-brief.md`,
# `backend-capabilities.md`. They existed on every working tree and in no commit, so
# the deployment 404'd on them and CI failed the drift check while every local run
# passed. Digests only ever land in `assets/`; nothing else here is hashed.
/priv/static/assets/*-[0-9a-f]*.*
/priv/static/**/*.gz
/priv/static/cache_manifest.json

# Dialyzer's PLT — a ~7 MB build artifact derived from OTP + deps. CI caches it on
# mix.lock rather than tracking it.
/priv/plts/

# Wallaby writes here on a failed feature test (and on demand). Artefacts of a
